from professional wrestling to hollywood  dave bautista is a man who can do it all  as one of the greatest professional  wrestlers of all time batista initially  rose to prominence with his storied  career in wwe competing in matches  against some of the sport's greatest  icons in the process he amassed an  impressive six world heavyweight  championship victories following a  phenomenal in-ring career bautista then  decided to hang up the boots and tackle  the world of acting following his  transition into tinsel town bautista  took roles in a number of low-budget  direct-to-video films such as wrong side  of town and the scorpion king 3 battle  for redemption before landing his big  break in 2014's guardians of the galaxy  starring his tracks to destroyer  bautista quickly made a name for himself  in the marvel cinematic universe with  his portrayal of the lovable yet  tragedy-stricken giant his people are  completely literal metaphors are going  to go over his head nothing goes over my  head my reflexes are too fast i would  catch it since then bautista has played  drax in a number of marvel films  including the mega blockbuster avengers  end game on playing drax bautista told  collider i can just relate to drax so  much it's not even funny simple things  like the tattoos the tragedy because you  know i had a bit of tragedy in my life  as well so it's really easy for me to  pull from that indeed bautista didn't  achieve the success he enjoys without  having endured a little adversity along  the way in fact the star had a  tumultuous upbringing characterized by  economic hardship and violence bautista  grew up amidst the crime wave that swept  washington dc in the 1980s for example  as a child he once saw a man beaten up  and almost thrown from the overpass from  his doorstep and also once witnessed his  own mother being attacked though those  incidents were traumatic in and of  themselves there is one event that truly  stands out from bautista's terrifying  childhood one afternoon as bautista his  sister and a number of kids were  blissfully playing outside his mother  noticed that something was off as it  turned out there was a dead body lying  outside their home the police had been  called after the unnamed man was shot to  death but were taking too long to show  up bautista his sister and the  neighborhood children however had become  so desensitized to death that the body  didn't even seem to phase them that was  the moment in which donna rae finally  drew the line she subsequently moved her  children to san francisco california in  hopes of a better life and while life in  california might have been better for a  number of reasons the bautista family's  political leanings made it a  particularly apt new home dave bautista  who is an unwavering democrat is not the  only member of his family who leans left  his mother was cut from the same cloth  she was born and raised in a highly  conservative greek american home and was  later shunned for her leftist ideologies  on top of that bautista's mother was  also open about her relationships with  women much to her family's chagrin  despite this donna rae worked incredibly  hard as a single mother to support the  young bautista and his sister moving  them across the nation and working a  night job to pay the bills it appears  that rey's fierce loyalty and caring  nature has spilled over into bautista  himself having once described himself as  the proud son of a lesbian the wrestler  turned actor revealed in an interview  with the tampa bay times that his father  never did anything for him this in turn  led to him developing a protective  spirit over his mother and this has  extended to his champion of lgbtq plus  rights bautista has often taken to  twitter to passionately defend the lgbtq  plus community and admonish anyone who  might have an issue with that he even  once called out boxing legend manny  pacquiao for espousing anti-gay remarks  in a scathing and profanity-laden 